WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.080
Speaker 1: All right.

00:00:01.080 --> 00:00:04.600
An extraordinarily explosive story yesterday,
the details of which we don't still fully

00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:05.600
understand.

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:09.460
Donald Trump came out yesterday and claimed
that his passports had been seized by the

00:00:09.460 --> 00:00:13.640
FBI as they served the search warrant at his
Mar a Lago home last week.

00:00:13.640 --> 00:00:19.380
Now, if that is true, it indicates that the
FBI presumably sees Donald Trump as a flight

00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:24.140
risk and is worried about him leaving the
country, and thus they have removed his means

00:00:24.140 --> 00:00:25.990
of being able to leave the country.

00:00:25.990 --> 00:00:27.369
That would be a really big deal.

00:00:27.369 --> 00:00:33.250
It would be unprecedented for a former president
to be unable to leave the country.

00:00:33.250 --> 00:00:34.730
But is that actually what happened?

00:00:34.730 --> 00:00:35.730
Was it a mix up?

00:00:35.730 --> 00:00:36.730
Did Trump lie?

00:00:36.730 --> 00:00:38.630
We're still trying to figure it out.

00:00:38.630 --> 00:00:42.090
It started with Donald Trump posting untruth,
social.

00:00:42.090 --> 00:00:43.090
Quote.

00:00:43.090 --> 00:00:44.090
Wow.

00:00:44.090 --> 00:00:47.970
In the raid by the fbi of mar a lago, they
stole my three passports.

00:00:47.970 --> 00:00:50.520
One expired along with everything else.

00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:55.530
This is an assault on a political opponent
at a level never seen before in our country.

00:00:55.530 --> 00:00:57.170
Third world.

00:00:57.170 --> 00:01:00.760
Now, is it actually what happened?

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:07.600
We don't really know because there was a statement
late last night that the FBI is not in possession

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:12.150
of the passports now is not in possession
is a statement about the right then?

00:01:12.150 --> 00:01:14.760
It's not a statement about we never had them.

00:01:14.760 --> 00:01:18.550
It just means we don't have them at this exact
point in time.

00:01:18.550 --> 00:01:28.710
We later found out about an email that was
sent from someone in law enforcement, presumably

00:01:28.710 --> 00:01:34.310
to people on Trump's side, saying, We have
learned that the filter agents seized three

00:01:34.310 --> 00:01:39.670
passports belonging to President Trump, two
expired and one being his active diplomatic

00:01:39.670 --> 00:01:40.670
passport.

00:01:40.670 --> 00:01:43.930
We are returning them and they will be ready
for pick up at 2 p.m. today.

00:01:43.930 --> 00:01:47.530
I'm traveling, but you can coordinate further
with whoever.

00:01:47.530 --> 00:01:48.530
Redacted.

00:01:48.530 --> 00:01:49.530
Copied above.

00:01:49.530 --> 00:01:53.670
Now if that was indeed JPM, it would make
the statement from the FBI last night accurate

00:01:53.670 --> 00:01:59.940
that they were not in possession of the passports,
but they had them at cert at a certain point.

00:01:59.940 --> 00:02:04.460
We later, I guess this morning got another
report from NBC News.

00:02:04.460 --> 00:02:10.140
Trump's passports returned after Mar a Lago
searched per DOJ official in a message on

00:02:10.140 --> 00:02:11.630
a social media platform.

00:02:11.630 --> 00:02:16.370
Trump said the FBI agents who searched his
home last week, quote, stole three passports,

00:02:16.370 --> 00:02:18.180
including one that he said was expired.

00:02:18.180 --> 00:02:22.700
The FBI acknowledged it had had the passports
the same day Trump said on his social media

00:02:22.700 --> 00:02:26.590
platform that they took them on August 8th.

00:02:26.590 --> 00:02:31.290
A Justice Department official said Trump's
passports have been returned, so we really

00:02:31.290 --> 00:02:35.400
don't know exactly what happened here.

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:38.060
Why was Trump looking for his passports?

00:02:38.060 --> 00:02:44.630
How did he know that they were in the boxes
that he claimed were planted by the FBI?

00:02:44.630 --> 00:02:49.510
I've never gone looking for my passport when
I wasn't planning to leave the country as

00:02:49.510 --> 00:02:52.060
a sort of curiosity.

00:02:52.060 --> 00:02:59.150
It's all very strange, but it does not appear
that the overall intention of the FBI was

00:02:59.150 --> 00:03:03.470
to semi permanently prevent Donald Trump from
leaving the country.

00:03:03.470 --> 00:03:05.650
That would be a major, major thing.

00:03:05.650 --> 00:03:08.340
Why did they take the passports and give them
back?

00:03:08.340 --> 00:03:13.220
Was it an accident where the passports in
these particular boxes?

00:03:13.220 --> 00:03:14.380
We don't know.

00:03:14.380 --> 00:03:20.790
But it's all very, very strange

